    <contentRows>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "dd183f78-7d69-4eda-9b4c-a25970583a28",
      "key": "a047d8fc-de90-47e3-9b6f-9c504061d52a",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003E\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;\u0026lt;strong\u0026gt;canonical_url:\u0026lt;/strong\u0026gt; \u0026quot;\u0026lt;a href=\u0026quot;https://www.addact.net/blogs/umbraco-17-lts-features-and-future\u0026quot; rel=\u0026quot;noopener noreferrer\u0026quot;\u0026gt;https://www.addact.net/blogs/umbraco-17-lts-features-and-future\u0026lt;/a\u0026gt;\u0026quot;\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Every few years, the digital ecosystem takes a big leap forward. Frameworks evolve, performance expectations increase, and businesses look for platforms that can modernize without disrupting their existing operations.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;For teams building with Umbraco, this evolution has always felt steady and intentional \u2014 each release improving the editing experience, strengthening stability, and simplifying the development workflow.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;With the launch of Umbraco 17, the newest Long-Term Support (LTS) edition, the platform reaches another important milestone. It\u0026#39;s not a radical reinvention but a strategic continuation of everything Umbraco does well: usability, flexibility, and long-term reliability.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;\u0026lt;strong\u0026gt;Why Umbraco 17 Matters\u0026lt;/strong\u0026gt;\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Umbraco 17 is the next LTS after version 13 \u2014 and the upgrade path is intentionally smooth.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;If you\u2019re on Umbraco 13, you can directly upgrade to 17.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;All intermediate migrations are applied automatically.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;No multi-step upgrade headaches.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;This is especially valuable for enterprise teams that prioritize stability and predictable lifecycles.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Built on .NET 10 LTS, Umbraco 17 aligns with Microsoft\u2019s support timeline and will receive security \u002B patch updates until late 2028. That gives organizations a strong, future-ready foundation for planning and compliance.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Major Advancements in Umbraco 17\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;h2\u0026gt;\n  \n  \n  1. Load-Balanced Backoffice\n\u0026lt;/h2\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Umbraco 17 introduces true backoffice load balancing, allowing editors across regions to work simultaneously without:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;performance drops\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;content conflicts\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;task failures \nIt especially improves long-running operations and real-time features like SignalR.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;h2\u0026gt;\n  \n  \n  2. Consistent UTC Date \u0026amp;amp; Time Zone Handling\n\u0026lt;/h2\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Older Umbraco versions relied on server-local time, causing issues for:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;multi-region deployments\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;daylight-saving differences\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;workflows or scheduled publishing\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Umbraco 17 fixes this with:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;All system dates stored in UTC\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Automatic migration for historical data\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;A new Date-Time with Time Zone property editor\nScheduling, content workflows, and integrations become far more reliable.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;h2\u0026gt;\n  \n  \n  3. Improved Backoffice UI \u0026amp;amp; Editor Experience\n\u0026lt;/h2\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;The editorial experience gets a noticeable polish:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Clearer and more consistent entity icons\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Streamlined navigation\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Accessibility improvements\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Subtle but meaningful speed boosts\nIt\u0026#39;s not flashy, but it makes editing faster and more intuitive.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;h2\u0026gt;\n  \n  \n  4. Stronger Extension Model\n\u0026lt;/h2\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Since the switch to the Bellissima backoffice (v14), Umbraco has been moving toward a modern extensible architecture.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;In version 17:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Extensions are now first-class\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Upgrade predictability improves\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Reusable components become more stable\nThis is a big win for teams who rely on custom editors, dashboards, or integrations.\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Umbraco 17 on Cloud: Built for Scale\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\nUmbraco Cloud gets several enhancements tailored to enterprise environments:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Better CI/CD tooling\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Hostname validation\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Centralized identity management\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Bandwidth insights\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Reliable scaling for high-traffic workloads\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Plus, Umbraco Engage now aligns with the new backoffice and supports Deploy, making personalization moves across environments seamless.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Developer-Focused Enhancements\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\nUmbraco 17 brings upgrades that directly improve engineering workflows:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;TipTap becomes the default rich-text editor\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Server-side preview URLs\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Optimized dependency layer for .NET 10\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Faster Models Builder performance\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Together, these reduce debugging friction and improve day-to-day development speed.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Installing Umbraco 17 (Quick Guide)\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\nYou\u2019ll need:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;.NET 10 or later\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;VS Code or Visual Studio 2022\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;SQLite or SQL Server (2016\u002B)\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;A modern browser\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://dev.to/addact_technologies_3322b/umbraco-17-lts-features-improvements-what-developers-should-know-234d\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
